    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18851" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">frontōsus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		2. frons, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>manybrowed</i>, <i>having several
				foreheads.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, said of Janus: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">frontosior,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aug. Civ. D. 1, 4 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>that has a bold
				forehead</i>, <i>shameless</i> (late Lat.), <i><span class="en">Aug. Serm. in Psa. 1, 68</span></i>.</div>
